    A12-1 — reduce the padding ABOVE the section title so the title sits closer to the top of the section boundary.
    A12-2 — increase the padding BELOW the title so there is more space before the first related-record line.
    A12-3 — add MORE horizontal space between the record NUMBER and the record NAME (W11 task 112 bumped it to
      `spacingHorizontalS`; increase further — e.g. `spacingHorizontalM` or a fixed gap — so they are clearly separated).
    A12-4 — the on-form collapsed-card "matched by/because …" reason line (kept in W11): INCREASE its font size (from
      the current small size to ~`fontSizeBase200`→`fontSizeBase300` range, matching the row text scale) and REMOVE
      the italic styling. Do NOT remove the line — just restyle it (larger, non-italic).

    Apply the refined title padding via Fluent tokens (ADR-021). Since this asymmetric title padding (small top /
    larger bottom) is now the Spaarke convention, ALSO update `docs/standards/UI-DESIGN-STANDARDS.md` to record it
    (title: reduced top padding, increased bottom padding — name the tokens used).
  </prompt>

  <goal>
